    "en": "The Place des Martyrs (Martyrs' Square) is an important memorial site in Cotonou. It was established to honor the Beninese citizens who lost their lives defending the country against a mercenary attack on January 16, 1977. The square's central monument depicts a determined soldier, symbolizing the courage and spirit of resistance of the Beninese people. The square is not only a place of remembrance but also serves as an important public space for national ceremonies and events. It reminds the nation of the importance of sovereignty and the sacrifices made to preserve it."
