      en: "The Resistance Monument in Natitingou commemorates the local population's struggle against French colonial rule in the late 19th century. Inaugurated in 1995, it stands on Place de la Résistance in Natitingou. The monument consists of a group of three stone pillars, each representing the resistance movements of the Ditammari, Gulmacheba, and Waama ethnic groups. The pillars are 6 meters tall and adorned with symbolic sculptures. A small park with explanatory panels about the history of resistance surrounds it.",
